repository-code: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-graphics-python
url: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-graphics-python
abstract: >-
  A model of how the Super Nintendo reads graphics: bitplane tiles at every
  depth, tilemaps, the object attribute table, palettes in fifteen bit colour,
  and the mode 7 affine transform. Every case is settled exhaustively rather than
  by sampling, because the input space of a tile decoder is small enough to walk
  in full.
keywords:
  - emulation
  - super-nintendo
  - graphics
  - mode-7
  - tilemap
  - hardware-model
  - conformance
